From: DBY-W09 Stage-A implementation
Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] dt-bindings: ufs: allow one or two SM8250 power domains

The generic dt-schema converter treats maxItems without minItems as an
exact-length tuple. ROUND36 raises the shared maxItems to two for SM8250,
which unintentionally turns the existing one-domain SM8250 topology into
an invalid fixture. State the lower bound explicitly; the SM8250 conditional
then permits one or two domains while the non-SM8250 branch remains exactly one.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs-common.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs-common.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs-common.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs-common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs-common.yaml
@@ -43,2 +43,3 @@
   power-domains:
+    minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2

--
